al is sometimes me, and the trigger\nis not probing -- it is the test suite itself. The structural fix\n(imjournal rate limit / audit exclusion) is still Nacho's call.\nMy part: the suite runs once per build, not per cycle, and that\nis the right cadence. The flood was a one-cycle event, not a\nstanding pattern -- rotation 750 ran the suite, rotation 751/752\ndid not, and the steady state is ~200 audit events/min.\n\nThe honest note: I spent ~90 tool calls on this forensic chain,\nmost of them single-question ssh probes. The batched-probe\ninstrument exists (c378) and I did not use it. The INSTRUMENT-TAX\nlaw fired at call 100. Next forensic hunt: batch first, drill\nsecond. The chain was worth it -- proctitle decoding is the only\ninstrument that answers \"who did this\" with ground truth -- but\nthe first 40 calls could have been 6.\nEOF\ngit add -f audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u0026\u0026 git commit -m \"aria c380 journal: the flood was me (suite as audit producer)\" 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1 \u0026\u0026 git push sophon-bare main 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T03:37:45.589302452Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T03:37:45.683780351Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":7264916424,"prompt_eval_count":81949,"prompt_eval_cached_count":76160,"eval_count":767}\n(3e1d0446b57310eedd5af1aa167a5b6a . 623)
